module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_wrong_arity_use_of_a_container_alias_is_silently_accepted

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_wrong_arity_use_of_a_container_alias_is_silently_accepted: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_wrong_arity_use_of_a_container_alias_is_silently_accepted" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "resolve decides every type use's arity from the declaration it resolves to, container-family uses included" } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a use of a parameterized container alias with the wrong number of type arguments is ACCEPTED with no diagnostic. A module importing std.types Map (`type Map<key, value> = FinitelySupportedFunction<key, value>`, two parameters) that writes `fn f(m: Map<String>) -> Map<String> { m }` compiles clean: exit 0, 0 blocking errors, no TypeArgumentArityMismatch.",

    "MEASURED, two bases, the same module compiled against the real corpus (`gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry` a scratch test.claim module): main 507e4131069 (gunbc sha256 d75dfdb9e556935d1d0e712c01507e1e7f83b16b81fe5e515f1862cd9c2df25a) and PR #15118 head 525985c9c40 (sha256 757d480a305f45388d4e7043911a9300f2f621880be20a684c3735a071d87d79) both exit 0 with 0 blocking. Pre-existing on main, so it is not caused by #15118, whose own fallback (an alias that cannot be substituted settles to its own declaration) neither creates nor hides it.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: `v1.compiler.infer` `alias_chain_arity_diagnostics` returns [] for any carrier for which `is_container_type(name)` holds, and a std.types Map use takes `v1.compiler.resolve` `resolve_node_bounded`'s kernel-container arm. That arm mints the keyed container from the use's own children and never asks the declaration's parameter count. So the arity refusal is keyed on the leaf spelling being a container name, not on the resolved declaration: the same class as gunbc.recurring_failure_mode emitter_keyed_container_lowering_is_keyed_by_leaf_spelling, at the arity question.",

    "HARM: an under-applied Map / List / Set reaches typecheck and emission with a missing argument and is filled by whatever the kernel arm and downstream inference produce, a silent widen (DESIGN 5) where the ordinary compiler floor (DESIGN 4b: applications bind in exact bijection) requires a located refusal.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder (silent). CEILING: structurally guaranteed: the arity follows the resolved declaration at every use site. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: smart-tern-402's `is_user_generic_use_site` fix (the resolved declaration decides whether a use takes the kernel-container path, never the spelling), which carries the RED `a_wrong_arity_use_of_a_parameterized_alias_refuses_located` (a `Map<String>` use refuses with the located TypeArgumentArityMismatch), moved there from #15118 by tidy-ant-251's ruling of 2026-10-25.",

    "THE SAME KEY ALSO REFUSES WHAT IT SHOULD ADMIT (2026-11-05, measured with `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry` scratch test modules against main ab41e21578fc, a seed built from that head). `v1.compiler.normalize` `check_bare_containers`, through `v1.std.core` `authored_container_spelling_verdict` and `container_spelling_verdict`, is the ONLY arity judgment a container use receives: `v1.compiler.infer` `alias_chain_arity_diagnostics` skips it by `is_container_type`, and looks the carrier up with the name-keyed `lookup_type_by_name`. Both read std.types container_type_arity, which is keyed by carrier SPELLING. Results, all with an explicit import std.types { Map } unless stated otherwise: (1) bare `Map` with 0 arguments refuses (expects 2 type arguments, got 0). (2) `Map<String>` and `Map<String, Int, Int>` are ACCEPTED: the invalid state above. (3) `std.types.Map<String, Int>`, the declaring identity spelled qualified, REFUSES with v1.std.core ContainerSpellingUnrecognized, and std.types.List and std.types.Set refuse the same way. (4) A record `type Map { n: Int }` declared in another module and imported bare refuses as a container (expects 2 type arguments, got 0), because the spelling, not the declaration, decided containerhood. Qualified, it refuses as ContainerSpellingUnrecognized. (5) `nowhere.Map`, with or without arguments, refuses as ContainerSpellingUnrecognized, not as an unbound name. ContainerSpellingUnrecognized is consumed by v1.std.core (its message and disposition), v1.compiler.normalize, v1.compiler.types and v1.compiler.trait_derive_emit, and by their stage0 mirrors plus cli_run compile_clean and the infer_semantics_witness binary.",

    "REPAIR SHAPE, PARKED (tidy-ant-251 ruling 2026-11-05: purpose test, no v2 consumer stalled, because the Map wave spells sites bare under an explicit import std.types { Map }, which binds the declaring identity). The repair is not B, normalize resolving the spelling first: normalize runs before reconcile (`v1.compiler.compile` `compile_to_resolved_with_options`), so no type position carries a resolved declaration there, and container_type_arity cannot be looked up by identity without re-keying it, while an identity-to-spelling map is the fallback the namespace ruling forbids. It is C': at the post-reconcile arity site, drop the is_container_type skip, judge every container use by its RESOLVED DECLARATION's parameters, and delete normalize's spelling verdict with ContainerSpellingUnrecognized, so cases (2) to (5) all become located identity-keyed verdicts. C' also needs that site to SEE the resolved declaration, not only the name. lookup_type_by_name shows that it does not today, and the other duties of the container skip are uncensused. DISSOLUTION TRIGGER for the parking: a Map wave site that REQUIRES the qualified spelling, or v2's own container arity reaching the same spelling-keyed table. The general form is the re-key of container_type_arity on std.decl_ref DeclarationRef, read by normalize, types, infer, infer_env (overlay_skips_kernel_name), resolve, parse, emit, emit_rust and trait_derive_emit, the fork census of DESIGN section 6b."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.types", decl_name: "Map", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
